After a rather uneventful game that started out quite as usual, I had a
tame soldier ant pop out of my pack, and things began to look up. I
named him Sparky after my ant from the game before, who didn't manage
to save me from my own foolishness in pressing 'x' instead of 'z' to
teleport myself out of danger. As in last game, I dragged Sparky around
the mines, and had him kill a few guards in Minetown, but a sad feeling
passed over me while I was returning to the main dungeons, so I just
decided to return to Minetown and pick up my pet shapeshifter (courtesy
of my starting spell, charm monster!). There a wild soldier ant
threatened to rend me apart, but I was able to tame him as soon as I
restored my mana in the empty level below.
     Of course, I named him Sparky, too.
So I went back to the chaotic temple there to b'u'c some items there,
but myself being neutral, I was unable to sacrifice items there.
Outside, I found that my pet baluchitherium had just ripped apart the
shopkeeper of the food shop next door. I took the coins and bought
proection from the priest. After waiting for quite a while, the
shapeshifter managed to change into something nasty again, and promptly
shredded the priest. I got a spellbook of create monster, a + of
stone-to-flesh, a blessed +0 robe, and my 3200 coins back, plus some
additional change.
     So, why not finish the job? Between Sparky and the shapeshifter (I
didn't name him so that the attacking prompt would show what he turned
into), the Minetown watch was ravaged and eaten, and all of the
shopkeepers met the same fate. (Yes, Izsack too, fell to the wrath of
an arch-lich, disenchanter, and some other large creature...) The watch
captain, who was the last to go, left me a pair of old gloves, a silver
sabre and a crystal plate mail, but due to my wizard's nerdy
composition, I had to drop my duplicate wands, potions, and other
pieces of armour just in order to wear the robe, the gloves, and the
crystal mail.
     As I also left my CoMR in my stash, I had to use create monster to
sacrifice until I recieved Magicbane for the magic resistnace. Also due
to weight, I couldn't carry my silver sabre or my starting quarterstaff
(which I did not enchant any further). A leash was also out of the
question, and the tool shop only carried a trio of tin whistles. The
only yellow ) that was in the lighting shop was a brass lantern, and
the only useful ) I stumbled on in the mines was a magic marker
(charges unid'd). It might be difficult to bring both creatures with
me, and if I can only take one, I'm not sure which one to bring:
soldier ants rip apart small creatures with ease (and so can I), but
are wimpy against anything larger. The shapeshifter seems to be limited
to about 15 forms or so, and although some of these are really
powerful, most of them are slow and pathetic -- "You stop. Your
woodchuck is in the way!".
     So, what should I do now? Without a bag of holding, I have to
leave my additional items behind. Without a magic whistle, I might also
have to leave my pets behind. I'm not sure if I can survive later in
the dungeons like this, with limited spells and items. Any suggestions?



